     ],
     "text": "All characteristics and comparisons are from comparative"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      35.52,
      285.84,
      270.96,
      294.24
     ],
     "text": "growing trials conducted at Emerald in Victoria between"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      35.52,
      296.64,
      271.2,
      305.76
     ],
     "text": "March 1990 and March 1992. Growing conditions were the"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      35.52,
      308.16,
      270.96,
      316.8
     ],
     "text": "same as would be used in commercial production. One hundred"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      35.04,
      318.96,
      270.96,
      327.84
     ],
     "text": "plants of the variety were grown in 200 mm containers for two"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      35.28,
      330.0,
      270.96,
      338.88
     ],
     "text": "seasons in a typical pine bark and sand based medium enriched"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      35.28,
      341.28,
      270.96,
      348.48
     ],
     "text": "with time release fertilizer. Plants were raised outside and"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      35.28,
      352.32,
      270.72,
      360.96
     ],
     "text": "spaced to allow full development. Chemical treatment was"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      35.04,
      363.12,
      270.48,
      372.0
     ],
     "text": "used for fungal and pest control only. Measurements and obser-"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      35.04,
      374.16,
      270.72,
      382.8
     ],
     "text": "vations are from 10 specimens selected at random from the 100"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      34.8,
      384.96,
      117.12,
      393.84
     ],
     "text": "plants of each variety."
    }
   ],
   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "All characteristics and comparisons are from comparative\ngrowing trials conducted at Emerald in Victoria between\nMarch 1990 and March 1992. Growing conditions were the\nsame as would be used in commercial production. One hundred\nplants of the variety were grown in 200 mm containers for two\nseasons in a typical pine bark and sand based medium enriched\nwith time release fertilizer. Plants were raised outside and\nspaced to allow full development. Chemical treatment was\nused for fungal and pest control only. Measurements and obser-\nvations are from 10 specimens selected at random from the 100\nplants of each variety.",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "type": "text",
